# Page Section Workflow

## Core rule
- Build every screen **section by section**, never a full page in one task.
- For each section: **create the component first**, then use it on the screen.
- Do not start the next section until the user asks for it.
- Reuse shared composables/models when the shape already exists — see rule `reuse-shared-ui.mdc`.

## Live shop.app reference (required — non-negotiable)
- Screenshots in `docs/ui-reference/` are **not enough** for **shopper** screens.
- **Every time** the user asks to build, refine, or restyle shopper UI: open the **matching** page/section on **https://shop.app** in the agent browser first (e.g. `/categories` for Categories, `/products/{id}/{slug}` for Product detail — use the exact product URL when the user provides one) and fully inspect that section: layout, spacing, radii, typography, carousel/scroll behavior, interactions, and breakpoints.
- Measure compact and desktop (and mid when the pattern changes) before coding.
- User screenshots complement live inspection; they do **not** replace it.
- Do **not** mark shopper work done until live shop.app for that section was opened and the measured behavior is reflected in code.

### Merchant admin exception
- Admin screens (Create store, Add product, later edit/dashboard) are **not** shop.app storefront.
- Visual source of truth: `docs/ui-reference/admin/` (Shopify Admin screenshots). Do **not** open shop.app for these pages.
- Still verify responsive compact vs `desktopBreakpoint` (1024dp two-column on Add product) / `mdBreakpoint` (768dp on Create store) and card gaps in code.

## Required checks when adding a new section
Every new (or refined) **shopper** section **must** include live shop.app verification of:

1. **Responsive sizing** — measure compact and desktop (and mid if the pattern changes). Do not ship fixed card/row widths when shop.app scales with viewport (e.g. carousel `n`-up formulas, grid column counts, gaps). Apply the same behavior in Compose (`BoxWithConstraints` / breakpoint tokens as needed).
2. **Internal spacing** — title→content, item gaps, padding, radii from live inspection, not guesses.
3. **Gap above (critical)** — measure the distance from the **previous** section’s bottom content to this section’s top (title or first row). Match shop.app exactly when wiring into the screen. Prefer the page’s shared section gap token when one exists (Categories: `CategoriesSectionGap` = 40dp ↔ shop.app `space-y-space-40`); do not invent a different top/bottom pad that doubles or collapses that rhythm.
4. **Gap below** — only if this section owns trailing space before the next block; otherwise let the screen / next section own the shared gap.

Do **not** mark a shopper section done until responsive sizes and the gap from the section above are checked on live shop.app and reflected in code. For admin sections, check compact vs `mdBreakpoint` and card gaps against `docs/ui-reference/admin/`.

## Current focus
- Active screen: **Add product** (merchant admin) — `CreateProductScreen`, route `/admin/products/new`
- Visual reference: `docs/ui-reference/admin/create-product/` (Shopify Admin), not shop.app
- Single-page two-column form from 1024dp: basics, media, category, price, inventory, shipping, variants + combination table, SEO accordion; sticky status/organization rail. Default status Draft. Mock-only; no purchase flow.
- Create store (`CreateStoreScreen`, `/admin/stores/new`) remains complete; only touch it when wiring Visit store or Add product.
- Shopper Store / Shop (`StoreScreen`, `/m/{shopId}`) remains complete for its listed sections; only touch it when wiring Visit store or shared chrome.
- Product detail remains complete for its listed sections.
- Categories screen remains complete for its listed sections; only touch it when wiring product/shop clicks or shared chrome.
- Categories vertical rhythm: `CategoriesSectionGap` (40dp) between major blocks on `CategoriesScreen`

## Placement
- Reusable pieces: `shared/.../ui/components/`
- Admin form primitives: `shared/.../ui/components/admin/`
- Admin create-store / create-product sections: `shared/.../ui/sections/admin/`
- App chrome navigation: `shared/.../ui/navigation/`
- Categories sections: `shared/.../ui/sections/categories/`
- Product detail sections: `shared/.../ui/sections/product/`
- Store sections: `shared/.../ui/sections/store/`
- Screen assembly: `shared/.../ui/screens/CreateProductScreen.kt` (active), `CreateStoreScreen.kt`, `StoreScreen.kt`, `ProductDetailScreen.kt`, `CategoriesScreen.kt`, `HomeScreen.kt`
- Shell: `shared/.../ui/shell/AppShell.kt`, `AppContentContainer.kt`

## Visual reference
- Shopper screens: `docs/ui-reference/` screenshots **and** live shop.app. Match shop.app look with Persian RTL and `VitranTheme`.
- Admin screens: `docs/ui-reference/admin/` only (Shopify Admin cards, black primary, light gray page). Persian RTL still applies.
- Do **not** use Material3 `NavigationBar` / `NavigationRail` for app chrome.

## When to use
- Always, for any screen/section UI work in this repo.

## When to update
- Active screen changes (e.g. leave Product detail for Deals).
- Product detail or Categories section order changes.
- Shared section-gap token or page rhythm changes.
- Package paths for components/screens settle or move.
